with scene('09-corrections-rejection','05-reraise','Raise a fresh request from a rejected one','Riya can use Raise it again after obtaining fresh authorisation. This action creates and submits a new request from the rejected details; it does not reopen the rejected record. Notice the new request number on the confirmation. The previous rejection remains in history, and the new request still needs its own manager decision.', 'View this request'):
 goto('/requests/3');click('button','Raise it again')
with scene('09-corrections-rejection','06-new-number','Verify the new approval cycle','The new request is awaiting approval. Its history identifies that it was raised again from the rejected request, keeping the relationship traceable. Review the copied details and edit them while pending if the fresh authorisation changes the scope or amount. Reraising copies the request information; it does not provide automatic approval or proof of payment.', 'Awaiting approval'):
 click('link','View this request')
with scene('18-withdraw-cancel','05-renewed-request','Submit a cancellation with confirmed facts','Later the supplier confirms that the order really has been cancelled. Riya sends a new cancellation request with that updated reason. This demonstrates that a declined cancellation does not erase the option to raise a justified new one while the approved request remains unpaid. The payment freeze applies again until Mira decides.', 'Cancellation requested'):
 goto('/requests/10');click('link','Request cancellation');fill('Reason','Supplier has now confirmed the order is cancelled and no invoice remains payable. Please close this unpaid request.');click('button','Send cancellation request');goto('/requests/10')
